course: dictionary
lesson: 14009
title: Shiny words: lustrous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Lustrous» is a describing word for something that shines softly and brightly, with a smooth glow. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The pearl had a lustrous glow.» A pearl is smooth and gleaming, so lustrous must mean shining with a soft glow.
explain: Scientists use lustrous in a special way. When a metal is polished or freshly cut, it has a shiny look called lustre. «Gold is lustrous, so it shines when it is cut.» A lustrous metal is one that shows that shine.
explain: Writers also use lustrous to paint a picture. «Her lustrous hair shone in the sun.» Lustrous is a richer word than shiny, so it tells the reader the hair looked smooth, healthy and glowing. Try swapping in shiny: the sentence still works, but it sounds plainer.
fact: «Lustrous» means shining softly and brightly, with a smooth glowing surface.
fact: Lustre is the shiny look that metals and some minerals have when they are polished or freshly cut.
fact: Geologists sort minerals by lustre: metallic, glassy, pearly and dull.
fact: Things that can be lustrous include pearls, silk, healthy hair, fur and polished metal.
fact: Lustrous is a rich describing word, so it can make a story more vivid than shiny.
exercise: «The pearl had a lustrous glow.» What does lustrous mean? | Heavy and hard to lift | Dark and cold | *Shining softly and brightly | Wet with rain
exercise: Why do scientists say metals are lustrous? | They are soft and wet | *They look shiny when they are polished | They always float on water | They are made of wood
exercise: «Her lustrous hair shone in the sun.» Find and copy one word that means shining. | sun | *shone | hair
test: Geologists sort minerals by their lustre. Which one is a type of lustre? | Loud | Sweet | Heavy | *Metallic
test: «The cat had a lustrous coat.» What does this mean? | *Its fur shone softly and brightly | Its fur was very short | Its fur was dirty and dull | It had no fur at all
exam: Which phrase describes a freshly polished silver spoon? | barely a whisper | *lustrous metal | curt reply | glum face
